**Read:** [Corrosion current — Derek H. Lister](../sources/Corrosion-Current-Lister.lingua#r_13M9DHG16SHQ1WG0C46CADMMD5), [Corrosion control and interpretation of tests — NPL](../sources/Corrosion-and-Test-Interpretation-NPL.lingua#r_6SEQ1G67MES2K0JB6X7AEA4WD6) and [Prevention of hydrogen embrittlement in steels — Bhadeshia](../sources/Hydrogen-Embrittlement-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_1VT41JGPGJ3NGXT47VKG1DFCT4) in full; use complete primary methods for the chosen actual material and exposure.

Reconstruct polarization/transport and independent loss or cracking evidence for a specified microstructure and loading history. Independently reproduce the mixed-potential calculation, then derive any additional model needed for your case rather than extending its two branches by analogy. Compare kinetic, transport, passivation or hydrogen explanations using discriminating observations.

**Deliver:** Balanced reactions, current/material balances, justified parameter inference, uncertainty and a prediction for a changed area ratio, environment, surface state or loading condition. Analyze a test-to-service mismatch using Turnbull's critique. Defend how an intervention changes the mechanism and what further evidence is needed before claiming a useful service improvement. Revise the investigation after a substantive alternative interpretation.

